    <text>string processing techniques the internal organization of
    string processing systems is discussed. six techniques for data
    structures are presented and evaluated on the basis of: (1)
    creation of strings; (2) examination of strings; and (3)
    alteration of strings. speed of operation, storage
    requirements, effect on paging, and programmer convenience are
    also considered. one of the techniques, single-word linked
    blocks, is used in an example demonstrating an implementation
    of a snobol string processing language on an ibm system/360.
    july, 1967 madnick, s. e. ca670703 jb february 28, 1978 9:04
    am</text>
