    <text>toward a discipline of real-time programming programming
    is divided into three major categories with increasing
    complexity of reasoning in program validation: sequential
    programming, multiprogramming, and real-time programming. by
    adhering to a strict programming discipline and by using a
    suitable high-level language molded after this discipline, the
    complexity of reasoning about concurrency and execution time
    constrain ts may be drastically reduced. this may be the only
    practical way to make real-time systems analytically verifiable
    and ultimately reliable. a possible discipline is outlined and
    expressed in terms of the language modula. august, 1977 wirth,
    n. multiprogramming, real-time programming, process
    synchronization, processor sharing, program validation, modula
    3.80 4.22 ca770805 jb december 28, 19777:39 am</text>
