    <recordId>592</recordId>
    <text>microprocessors in personal informational systems.
    powerful microcomputer systems have become available at a cost
    which many individuals and small libraries can afford.
    discusses present and near-term future capabilities of
    microcomputers for personal information systems and
    requirements for such systems. examines currently available
    hardware and software in terms of these requirements, also
    current trends.</text>
  </DOC>
