    <text>information-related bills introduced in the u.s. senate.
    5 new bills-the public telecommunications act, national driver
    register act, television licensing and renewal act, equal
    access to communications act, and hearing impaired tax
    incentive act-have been read in the us senate and assigned to
    the appropriate committees for action. describes each act
    briefly, and its relevance to the world of information.</text>
