    <text>th-century technology and the jefferson papers.ad apted
    from a paper presented at the modern technology and historical
    editing' national historical publications and records
    commission word processing conference, philadelphia,
    pennsylvania, 5 may 81. describes the preparation on the
    computer of the text and cumulative index of the multi-volume
    2papers of thomas jefferson1 through the cooperation of the
    project's editors and publisher with the computer centre at
    princetown university.</text>
