    <recordId>793</recordId>
    <text>region and the current system the complete equilibrium
    equation for the electron density in a solar controlled
    ionospheric region includes a term which depends on vertical
    drift and is usually neglected the layer critical frequency is
    then related to the zenith angle by the equation where is a
    constant and for an isothermal region has the value for
    recombination and for attachment values of deduced from actual
    observations lie between and these findings are discussed on
    the assumption that the variation of results from neglect of
    the vertical drift term the theory is supported by observations
    of singularities in the noon curves of latitude for several
    longitudes these singularities corresponding to normal values
    of coincide approximately with the position of the foci of the
    current system</text>
  </DOC>
