    press; peter lewis, british library; gordon graham,
    butterworths; and julian blackwell of blackwells spoke on the
    influence of the new technology on publishing and bookselling
    in the future.</text>
  </DOC>
  <DOC>
    <recordId>890</recordId>
    <text>integral equations of immunology the inversion of a
    particular integral equation of the first (fredholm) kind is
    the basic problem considered. the strategy which yielded
    success consisted of three essential points: (1) fit the known
    experimental data by a curve with properties which derive from
    properties of the (as yet unknown) function; (2) stabilize the
    computation for the unknown function by using singular value
    decomposition; (3) constrain the unknown function approximation
    (since it represents a probability distribution) to be
    nonnegative. a number of test cases are presented. one set of
    actual experimental data is analyzed with the procedures
    presented. october, 1972 hanson, r. j. integral equations of
    the first kind, nonnegative constraints, singular value
    analysis 3.10 5.14 5.18 5.41 ca721003 jb january 27, 1978 3:37
    pm</text>
