    <recordId>1126</recordId>
    <text>digital computer determination of alpha source activity a
    technique is described for determining the activity and
    homogeneity of an alpha source. it is believed that the
    technique, using a digital computer, has many uses and
    applications in the field of nuclear physics. the technique
    involves computer manipulation of the digital image of the
    nuclear source. experimental details are given. january, 1964
