    <recordId>1751</recordId>
    <text>a buddy system variation for disk storage allocation a
    generalization of the buddy system for storage allocation is
    described. the set of permitted block sizes {size(i)}, i=0,n,
    must satisfy the condition size(i)=size(i-1)+size(i-k(i)) where
    k may be any meaningful integral-valued function. this makes it
    possible to force logical storage blocks to coincide with
    physical storage blocks, such as tracks and cylinders. july,
    1976 burton, w. buddy system, dynamic storage allocation 3.89
    4.32 4.39 ca760708 jb january 4, 1978 11:24 am</text>
