    that american archival theory does not exist as a
    systematically formulated body of ideas but is an aggregation
    of ideas drawn from well-tested and widely accepted european
    archival principles and of pragmatic concepts developed to meet
    special needs of american archival administration and
    democratic traditions.</text>
