    <text>some factors influencing choice of host systems. choosing
    a suitable on-line host system is becoming an increasingly
    complex procedure. a set of criteria is suggested as a
    framework to help in decision making. the importance of
    identifying the specific needs of the user is stressed and the
    matching of these requirements to considerations such as range
    of data bases offered, command language, methods of access as
    well as economics and quality of service is examined.</text>
