    to derive estimates of the number of full-time programmers
    employed during the years 1969 through 1973. the 1973 figure of
    180,000 is considerably less than suggested in earlier reports.
    it is recommended that educational administrators consider
    whether the many courses aimed at training programmers are
    justified on a vocational basis. october, 1974 gilchrist, b.
    weber, r. e. programmer, employment, 1970 census, area wage
