    <text>multiple terminals under user program control in a
    time-sharing environment user-written programs on the dartmouth
    time-sharing system can communicate with many remote terminals
    simultaneously and can control the interactions between these
    terminals. such programs can be written using standard input
    and output instructions in any language available on the
