    <recordId>3544</recordId>
    <text>preliminary report on a system for general space planning
    a computer language and a set of programs within that language
    are described which allow the formulating and solving of a
    class of space planning problems. the language is an extension
    of algol and includes means to represent spaces and objects, to
    manipulate them, and to test the resulting arrangements
    according to a variety of constraints. the algorithms used to
    solve problems expressed in this language rely on heuristic
    programming. both the language and the search algorithms are
    detailed. february, 1972 eastman, c. m. automated design,
    architecture, heuristic programs, space planning 3.20 3.40 3.64
    3.66 ca720202 jb january 31, 1978 4:35 pm</text>
  </DOC>
