    <text>description of basic algorithm in detab/65 preprocessor
    the basic algorithm for the conversion of decision tables into
    cobol code is contained in the generator portion of the
    detab/65 preprocessor. the generator analyzes a decision table
    and produces simple cobol conditional statements. core storage
    is saved by using queueing techniques and extensive indexing
    and also by outputting the code as it is generated, a line at a
    time. the only optimization attempted is the elimination of
    obviously unnecessary tests on certain conditions in the
    decision table. since the preprocessor and this language
    associated with it were developed for cobol users, the
    preprocessor was written in a modular form in required
    cobol-61. july, 1967 callahan, m. d. chapman, a. e. ca670709 jb
    february 28, 1978 8:33 am</text>
