    <recordId>8291</recordId>
    <text>some promises kept' the peterborough town library. traces
    the development of the public library in peterborough, new
    hampshire, the oldest tax-supported library in the world.
    describes the financing of the library since its foundation in
    1833, and discusses its budget for 1981, approximately 80% of
    which is accounted for by tax support.</text>
  </DOC>
