    <text>comparison of iterative methods for the calculation of
    nth roots three iterative methods for calculation of nth roots
    (including one proposed by the author) are compared in two
    ways: (1) theoretical convergence estimates are given. (2) a
    new macrocompiler which estimates machine running time is used
    to compare the running time of the three methods for a variety
    of input data. march, 1961 traub, j. f. ca610302 jb march 17,
