    <recordId>9662</recordId>
    <text>books at auction' the art of deaccessioning. the cost of
    maintaining a library collection is high. while librarians
    welcome bequests, they are worried about costly conditions such
    as keeping the bequest intact or not selling it. libraries are
    increasingly using outside subject experts to weed their
    collections. for reasons of propriety, most discarded books are
    sold at auctions. libraries also send valuable books and
    manuscripts to auctions to obtain funds for specific purposes.
    offers advice concerning the decision to weed a collection,
    explains the procedure for contacting a book auction house, and
    gives hints on the condition of the books.</text>
  </DOC>
