    <text>programming semantics for multiprogrammed computations
    the semantics are defined for a number of meta-instructions
    which perform operation essential to the writing of programs in
    multiprogrammed computer systems. these meta-instructions
    relate to parallel processing, protection of separate
    computations, program debugging, and the sharing among users of
    memory segments and other computing objects, the names of which
    are hierarchically structured. the language sophistication
