    <text>an improved algorithm for decentralized extrema-finding
    in circular configurations of processes this note presents an
    improvement to lelann's algorithm for finding the largest (or
    smallest) of a set of uniquely numbered processes arranged in a
    circle, in which no central controller exists and the number of
    processes is not known a priori. this decentralized algorithm
    uses a technique of selective message extinction in order to
    achieve an average number of message passes of order (n log n)
    rather than o(n2). may, 1979 chang, e. roberts, r.
    decentralized algorithms, distributed systems, operating
    systems 4.32 4.35 5.25 5.32 ca790502 dh june 5, 1979 2:35
    pm</text>
