    <text>a model for verification of data security in operating
    systems program verification applied to kernel architectures
    forms a promising method for providing uncircumventably secure,
    shared computer systems. a precise definition of data security
    is developed here in terms of a general model for operating
    systems. this model is suitable as a basis for verifying many
    of those properties of an operating system which are necessary
    to assure reliable enforcement of security. the application of
    this approach to the ucla secure operating system is also
