    (adaptive library management system), a tool for storing and
    manipulating bibliographic information with a varied selection
    of modules available for performing different operations.
    presents a broad description of the types of operation which
    can be carried out. the 2 basic functions of adlib are the
    cataloguing and retireval modules and the system can be built
