    <text>from the state librarian. discusses the budget cuts
    inflicted on the western australia library board in the 1980-81
    financial year, particularly the 10.24% cut in the book fund.
    stresses the importance of libraries in modern australian
    society and regrets that greater use of libraries and such
    severe cuts have coincided.</text>
