    <text>threaded code the concept of "threaded code" is presented
    as an alternative to machine language code. hardware and
    software realizations of it are given. in software it is
    realized as interpretive code not needing an interpreter.
    extensions and optimizations are mentioned. june, 1973 bell, j.
    r. interpreter, machine code, time tradeoff, space tradeoff,
