    <recordId>16956</recordId>
    <text>a comparison of multivariate normal generators three
    methods for generating outcomes on multivariate normal random
    vectors with a specified variance-covariance matrix are
    presented. a comparison is made to determine which method
    requires the least computer execution time and memory space
    when utilizing the ibm 360/67. all methods use as a basis a
    standard gaussian random number generator. results of the
    comparison indicate that the method based on triangular
    factorization of the covariance matrix generally requires less
    memory space and computer time than the other two methods.
    december, 1972 barr, d. r. sezak, n. l. random number
    generator, normal distribution, multivariate normal
