    <recordId>16990</recordId>
    <text>the reactive typewriter program 84-character keyboard
    including alphabetical upper and lower case for good
    readability. if the machine is restricted to only a single
    case, the lower case is preferred. the reactive typewriter
    should be portable. the reactive typewriter should operate over
    any commercially used, dial-type telephone (voice) or telegraph
    (telex) line or over leased (nondial) telegraph lines
    interchangeably. january, 1963 mooers, c. n. ca630118 es march
