    <recordId>17352</recordId>
    <text>does rationalisation mean cuts in staff?. local
    government reorganization increased the number of service
    points of kokkola public libraries. soon after the
    reorganization a new central library was obtained and the
    workload was increased greatly. twice the library service
    applied to the council for more staff and were turned down. in
    1980 the council decided to carry out an o&amp;m survey
    concentrating on the staff requirements. as a result it was
    recommended that 2 extra permanent staff and 5 part-time staff
    should be employed. the survey also made recommendation for 2
    further surveys: to see whether it would be advantageous to
    increase the use of centralised cataloguing services and to
    look at the division of labour.</text>
  </DOC>
