    <recordId>17740</recordId>
    <text>the public library in a free enterprise society. states
    that the free public library in its present form is a uniquely
    us institution, reflecting the nation's commitment to
    individual initiative and free enterprise-ready access to books
    for self-help and self-improvement has been perceived as
    essential to building character and self-reliance for
    generations. traces the vital role of public libraries in the
    lives of leading us inventors, businessmen, and industries and
    calls for support for libraries (through the proposed national
    library and information services act) in their present
    financially-strained circumstances.</text>
  </DOC>
