    <text>matrix computations with fortran and paging the
    efficiency of conventional fortran programs for matrix
    computations can often be improved by reversing the order of
    nested loops. such modifications produce modest savings in many
    common situations and very significant savings for large
    problems run under an operating system which uses paging.
    april, 1972 moler, c. b. matrix algorithms, linear equations,
    fortran, paged memory, virtual memory, array processing 4.22
