    <text>final examination scheduling a method for scheduling
    final examinations to yield a minimal number of student
    conflicts is described. the "minimization" is achieved by
    repetitively evaluating a nonlinear set of equations. imbeded
    in the process is a random or monte carlo selection of
    assignments. as in such heuristic techniques, the solution may
    not be optimum and many solutions may be found which yield
    locally minimal results. computer programs are described and
    empirical results given. august, 1964 broder, s. ca640817 jb
