    <text>non-print media-audio hardware and software. traces the
    development of audio hardware for commercial purposes and the
    cost-effective trade-offs from the technology which have been
    used in its adaptation for the print handicapped. briefly
    discussed are methods used in software preparation' high volume
    for libraries, medium volume for academic use and low volume
    for special information materials for private
    individuals.</text>
