    rotnac working group, data base in copenhagen, 18-20 nov 80.
    the following papers were presented. 'the development of an
    international bibliographic network system', by richard coward;
    'national library centres, the use of marc tapes', by karen
    lunde christensen; 'problems of coordinating different
    classification codes in one database', by rob kooyman;
    'authority control in automated bibliographic systems', by
    eigil balling; 'one data base and a variety of output', by ole
