    <text>public libraries in a japanese community. following a
    study placement in a japanese central public library in
    1978-79, a brazilian university librarian describes how the
    library has adapted its services to meet particular user needs.
    gives a sketch of the busy commercial centre and its active
    population, correlating their way of life with the library's
    provisions. details are given of the stock and facilities
    available, internal and external.</text>
  </DOC>
