    <text>th annual conference of the association of german factory
    libraries.al though some factory libraries have closed owing to
    economic problems, those remaining are clearly thriving,
    providing valuable assistance in the creation of leisure
    activities. topics discussed include' fairy tales and fantasy
    literature of the 1960s and 1970s, elements of which are now
    often found in the works of several distinguished authors;
    science fiction, which is often of little literary value; the
    literature of black africa and its conflict with other
    cultures; topicality in dictionaries; the introduction of new
    readers to the library, involving the improvement of
    catalogues, publicity for new accessions, seminars within the
    firm and contact with youth clubs.</text>
  </DOC>
  <DOC>
