    <text>hidden lines elimination for a rotating object a method
    is presented of determining which parts of three-dimensional
    objects are visible and which are invisible when the objects
    are rotated about some axis. this paper describes a polygon
    comparison scheme in which the relationships of two polygons
    can be classified into tree types, and also discusses how the
    relationship is changed for each pair of polygons under
    rotation about some axis. a rotation table is defined for each
    pair of polygons, which remains fixed as long as rotation is
    about one axis and provides a means of rapidly determining the
    visible and hidden line relationship between two polygons.
    additional work must be done to extend this approach to
    simultaneous rotation about several axes. april, 1972
    matsushita, y. hidden line problem, display programming,
    computer graphics, displays, graphics, computer drawn picture
    4.40 4.41 4.49 ca720404 jb january 31, 1978 1:40 pm</text>
