    <text>the freedom of information debate in australia. freedom
    of information has been a catchcry in australia for a decade
    now. despite persistent lobbying no enactment of legislation
    has been achieved. discusses a bill introduced into parliament
    in 1978, mentioning us and uk influences. an afterword
    describes progress of the bill through the senate.</text>
  </DOC>
