    <text>a selective traversal algorithm for binary search trees
    the problem of selecting data items from a binary search tree
    according to a list of range conditions is considered. the
    process of visiting a minimal number of nodes to retrieve data
    satisfying the range conditions is called selective traversal.
    presented in this paper is an algorithm for selective traversal
    which uses a tag field for each node in the tree. the algorithm
    is particularly useful and efficient when examination of data
    is more time consuming than examination of a tag field. june,
    1978 driscoll, j.r. lien, y.e. data retrieval, range
    conditions, binary search tree, tree traversal, selective
    traversal 3.74 5.24 5.25 ca780602 dh february 26, 1979 12:40
    pm</text>
