    <text>personnel management in libraries. explores the factors
    that motivate the members of library professional staff to
    perform their function of accumulation, preservation and
    dissemination of knowledge. part i deals with theoretical
    formulations of how to motivate staff to work most efficiently
    and part ii deals with putting these theories into practice and
    evaluating their effectiveness.</text>
  </DOC>
