    <text>microprogramming, emulators and programming languages the
    problem we have been concerned with is that of converting
    language to action - or intellectual energy to mechanical
    energy. the medium that we use for this purpose is language and
    therefore we are preoccupied with the subject of language. in
    the areas of language investigation we have concentrated first
    on formalizing syntax and then on semantics. march, 1966 greem,
    j. ca660318 es march 17, 1982 10:10 am</text>
