    <recordId>35163</recordId>
    <text>guides to teaching cobol the teaching of cobol can be
    divided into three main subject areas. they are the syntax of
    cobol, the use of such syntax in solving any given problem, and
    programming concepts. it is generally accepted that some
    knowledge of the hardware and computer logic must be possessed
    by the programmer. the teaching problem arises in determining
    how thoroughly a student must know the hardware and logic for
    that computer for which he will write cobol programs.
    unfortunately, historical data concerning students' programming
    proficiency is almost non-existent and, at best, difficult to
    measure. how then might we approach solving this problem? may,
    1962 greene, i. ca620510 jb march 20, 1978 1:44 pm</text>
  </DOC>
