    <recordId>35459</recordId>
    <text>the principle of economic efficiency in organisation of
    the higher education libraries and in their specialised
    information activity (in english and rumanian). the prompt
    supply of scientific information required by education,
    research and production, and reduction of research time are the
    ultimate aims of higher education libraries. proposes the
    reduction of 'dead time' in scientific research by' improvement
    of the reading conditions by prompt serving of the reader;
    keeping specialised stock in specialised libraries; shortening
    time devoted to bibliography development. suggests the most
    appropriate means of obtaining maximum efficiency in minimum
    time and with minimum effort.</text>
  </DOC>
