    <text>symbolic notations for statistical tables and an approach
    towards automatic system design the preparation of statistical
    tables is an important function of the data processing systems
    of some organizations, and a symbolic notation for the
    description of tables has been shown to be a useful aid to
    documentation. such a notation also provides the first step
    towards making automatic a tedious and time-consuming part of
    system design and programming in many computer applications.
    one notation is described and suggestions are made for the
    implementation of the larger goal. june, 1965 smith, b. w.
    ca650603 jb march 7, 1978 12:41 pm</text>
