    <text>breaking new ground at eurocentres. describes the
    eurocentre lee green, london-probably britain's most modern
    school of english as a foreign language. the multi-media
    resources department comprises a library/student resources
    centre (src) and listening centre, 2 language laboratories, a
    classroom fitted with colour, closed-circuit tv, a sound
    recording studio and an av workshop.</text>
  </DOC>
  <DOC>
    <recordId>37088</recordId>
    <text>transistorized pulse amplifier instead of pulse
    transformers drift transistors with high cut off frequencies
    are used in diode logic circuits with input pulses the total
    rise and fall times are less than the delay between input and
    output pulses varying from to according to load
    conditions</text>
  </DOC>
