    <recordId>37478</recordId>
    <text>observations of the van allen radiation regions during
    august and september part one results are given of a
    preliminary analysis of data obtained from equipment flown on
    explorer sixth in addition to the inner and outer zones a
    stable intermediate zone was detected the outer zone intensity
    showed a large decrease following a sudden commencement but
    subsequently increased to be greatly in excess of its prestorm
    level comparison is made with other measurements of the
    radiation zones</text>
