    <text>a list-type storage technique for alphameric information
    a method which is economic in terms of space and time is
    proposed for the storage and manipulation of character strings
    of arbitrary length in a fixed word-length computer. the method
    is illustrated in an application to algol-type identifiers in
    an algol-like block structure. august, 1963 bowlden, h. j.
    ca630804 jb march 13, 1978 8:45 pm</text>
