    <text>a fast storage allocator a fast storage bookkeeping
    method is described which is particularly appropriate for
    list-structure operations and other situations involving many
    sizes of blocks that are fixed in size and location. this
    scheme, used in the llllll or l6 (bell telephone laboratories
    low-level list language), makes available blocks of computer
    registers in several different sizes: the smaller blocks are
    obtained by successively splitting larger ones in half, and the
    larger blocks are reconstituted if and when their parts are
    simultaneously free. october, 1965 knowlton, k.c. ca651011 jb
    march 6, 1978 6:35 pm</text>
