    <text>a method of syntax-checking algol 60 a syntax checker was
    designed based on the syntax of algol as described in the algol
    60 report [communications of the acm, may, 1960]. since the
    definition of the elements of the language is recursive it
    seemed most desirable to design the syntax checker as a set of
    mutually recursive processors tied together by subroutines
    which perform certain bookkeeping functions. because of the
    recursive nature of the language and of the syntax checker the
    problem of recovery after an error required much attention. a
    method was devised which permits most programs to be checked
    completely despite errors. august, 1964 lietzke, m. p. ca640805
    jb march 9, 1978 7:24 pm</text>
