    <text>time sharing in a traffic control program the toronto
    traffic signal control system consists of a variety of
    logically distinct computer programs, all competing for machine
    time. to satisfy these demands, a time-sharing program has been
    written whose purpose is to execute, in the order of a
    predefined priority, the various subprograms within the
    real-time system. in this paper the more interesting aspects of
    the time-sharing program are outlined. november, 1964 green, l.
    e. s. ca641112 jb march 9, 1978 3:49 pm</text>
  </DOC>
