    <text>a terminal-oriented communication system this paper
    describes a system for full-duplex communication between a
    time-shared computer and its terminals. the system consists of
    a communications computer directly connected to the time-shared
    system, a number of small remote computers to which the
    terminals are attached, and connecting medium speed telephone
    lines. it can service a large number of terminals of various
    types. the overall system design is presented along with the
    algorithms used to solve three specific problems: local
    echoing, error detection and correction on the telephone lines,
    and multiplexing of character output. july, 1977 heckel, p. g.
    lampson, b. w. terminal system, error correction, multiplexing,
    local echoing, communication system, network 3.81 4.31 ca770704
